Japan in 2023 yields a dense source universe for Chapter 6B, especially around child policy, social protection, welfare administration, disability access, health system capacity, poverty/income, and labor conditions. The strongest documentary families are official Japanese government strategy and white-paper materials, plus OECD/UN/WHO/World Bank/ILO baselines and Reuters-local reporting on the child-policy package and its funding debates. Access is mixed: most official pages are open; some newspaper items and PDFs may later prove paywalled or blocked, but they remain candidates.

